# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. They are executed under WSL/Linux, where
# a CRLF shebang line fails with a confusing "bad interpreter: No such file or
# directory". On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true these would
# otherwise arrive as CRLF and every script in tests/install-regression/ would
# refuse to run.
#
# The shell assets under src/ks_gen/assets/ are read by Python with universal
# newlines before being embedded in a kickstart, so they are unaffected either
# way — but pinning them costs nothing and removes the question.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Kickstart/YAML fixtures the harness feeds to anaconda.
*.tmpl text eol=lf
